  "findings": [
    "Inventory, desktop build, plugin renderer, and loaded-plugin workflows passed. Quality failed on Ubuntu because the Electron audit observed a local index completion status instead of the completed retrieval result; macOS and Windows quality jobs passed.",
    "Rust CI failed on Ubuntu, macOS, Windows, and Rust 1.95 in egui_canvas_text_edit_preserves_stale_draft_and_requires_explicit_reload at crates/ui-egui/src/lib.rs:5667. All four failures asserted that canvas_text_edit_receiver was Some after clicking Reload Canvas; each job reported 108 passed and 1 failed.",
    "Obsidian round-trip failed on all three operating systems. Linux could not locate an accessible Canvas edit text-card ID field and the captured form was disabled while a watcher refresh was in progress. Windows read back only 28 characters of a 42-character draft. macOS timed out waiting for the saved Canvas text card. Screenshots showed the expanded editor's lower controls clipped below the 800x600 viewport on Windows and macOS.",
    "No vault mismatch was reported. The next correction adds visible scrolling and editor auto-scroll, waits for the correct Canvas text-edit log's watcher refresh to finish before interaction, and correlates Electron retrieval progress events with their request so late progress cannot overwrite the final result."
  ],
